          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Sikorsky's Legacy and Awards</strong><br>\nSikorsky's work earned him multiple awards, including the National Medal of Science. He is remembered as a pioneer who made substantial contributions to both fixed-wing and rotor-wing aircraft. His innovations in helicopter design have saved countless lives through their use in rescue operations and have become standard in helicopter construction.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sikorsky Aircraft Corporation</strong><br>\nThe company that Sikorsky founded grew to become a major aerospace manufacturer. The Sikorsky Aircraft Corporation continued to innovate, creating helicopters for a variety of uses, including the famous Black Hawk military helicopter. The company's commitment to quality and innovation reflects Sikorsky's original vision and dedication.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sikorsky's Personal Philosophy</strong><br>\nIgor Sikorsky was not just an engineer but also a philosopher of aviation. He believed that aviation could bring people together and improve lives. His vision for the future of flight was not limited to technology; he also considered the human aspect of aviation and its potential to change the world for the better.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
